{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Re-ran the phantom restart probe with its two events sharing one case label, so the comparison that the previous receipt left as unknown can be decided. The harness now emits the commit-phase case event and the restart result event both with case phantom_restart, and adds a phase field set to commit to distinguish the halves; the cluster, the injected store failure, the partition, the client command and the restart over the leader's own stores are unchanged. Local verification reproduces the earlier observation exactly: the AddVoter write fails while the latest configuration grows to three voters at index 3 over a log ending at 2, the leader keeps office through the phantom quorum and commits at index 4 with the committed peer's log still at 2, and the restart loads only A and B with two voters, the new server absent, the last stored index still 4 and the stored commit index zero. The request declares the commit-phase event as a prerequisite keyed on case, phase, the failed write, the phantom voter count and the successful apply, and asserts that the restarted node does not load the new server, which should now correlate and be evaluated rather than left open.\"}"}}
